---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import { CardHeading } from '../components/landing/WorkflowCard';
import { ListChecks, Puzzle, Wrench, BrainCircuit, Bot, GitPullRequest, MessagesSquare, GitBranch, Landmark } from 'lucide-react';
import data from '../data/tools.json';
import { siteEditUrl } from '../lib/site';
const contracts = Object.keys(data.contracts).length, substrates = Object.keys(data.substrates).length;
const neutrality = data.vendorNeutrality;
const DOC = '/docs/vendor-neutrality';
// The six independent axes, as the vendor-neutrality document lists them.
const axes = [
  { name: 'LLM backend', anchor: '1-llm-backend', icon: BrainCircuit, how: 'Any model, hosted or local.' },
  { name: 'Agentic harness', anchor: '2-agentic-harness', icon: Bot, how: 'Any agent that reads skills.' },
  { name: 'Forge and tracker', anchor: '3-forge-and-tracker', icon: GitPullRequest, how: 'Any forge or issue tracker.' },
  { name: 'Communication', anchor: '4-communication-channels', icon: MessagesSquare, how: 'Mail, chat and forums.' },
  { name: 'Source control', anchor: '5-source-control-vcs', icon: GitBranch, how: 'Git, Subversion, Fossil and more.' },
  { name: 'Governance', anchor: '6-project-governance', icon: Landmark, how: 'Your project’s own rules.' },
];
const coverage = (c: (typeof neutrality.contracts)[number]) =>
  c.class === 'agnostic' ? 'Neutral by construction'
  : c.class === 'single-org' ? `Single organization (${c.vendors.join(', ')})`
  : c.green ? `${c.vendors.length} backends` : `${c.vendors.length} backend; needs another`;
const ORG_LOGO: Record<string, string> = { ASF: '/vendor-logos/oak.svg' };
const familyName = (f: string) => f.replace(/-/g, ' ');
const skillsByOrg: Record<string, number> = data.skills.byOrg;
const orgSummary = (org: (typeof data.organizations)[number]) => {
  const skills = skillsByOrg[org.id] ?? 0;
  if (!org.tools.length && !skills && !org.families.length) return 'The baseline for projects without a formal organization: no extra vocabulary, framework defaults throughout.';
  const families = org.families.length ? `, and the ${org.families.map(familyName).join(' and ')} skill families` : '';
  return `${org.tools.length} organization-specific tools, ${skills} skills${families}.`;
};
// The three layers, each with its size and the page that lists it.
const layers = [
  { title: `${data.skills.total} skills`, href: '/docs/modes', icon: ListChecks,
    text: 'The workflows: what to check, prepare, and bring back for approval.' },
  { title: `${contracts + substrates} capabilities`, href: '/docs/labels-and-capabilities', icon: Puzzle,
    text: `The interfaces skills need: ${contracts} capability contracts, such as reading an issue or drafting mail, and ${substrates} low-level capabilities.` },
  { title: `${data.tools.length} tools`, href: '/tools', icon: Wrench,
    text: `The implementations for your tracker, model, or other service; ${data.implementedTotal} already implemented.` },
];
---
<ContentLayout editUrl={siteEditUrl('src/pages/architecture.astro')} title="How Magpie fits together" description="Skills describe the work. Tools connect that work to your agent, services, and project conventions.">
  <div class="arch-flow" aria-label="Skills request capabilities implemented by tools">{layers.map(layer => <a href={layer.href} class="surface-card workflow-card card-link arch-card"><CardHeading title={layer.title} linkArrow><layer.icon slot="icon" aria-hidden="true" /></CardHeading><p>{layer.text}</p></a>)}</div>
  <section id="vendor-neutrality">
    <h2>Choose your tools without rewriting the workflow</h2>
    <p>Skills ask for a capability rather than a named vendor. Tools implement each capability for a backend, so your project can change its tracker, mail, model or agent while keeping the workflow. Neutrality holds on six independent axes; a choice on one never constrains the others.</p>
    <p class="arch-score"><strong>{neutrality.overall.green} of {neutrality.overall.total}</strong> capability contracts ({neutrality.overall.percent}%) have at least {neutrality.minVendors} backends or are neutral by construction. <strong>{neutrality.skills.neutral} of {neutrality.skills.total}</strong> skills are vendor-neutral{neutrality.harness && <>, and <strong>{neutrality.harness.neutral} of {neutrality.harness.total}</strong> low-level tools work with any agent</>}.</p>
    <div class="arch-flow arch-axes" aria-label="The six axes of vendor neutrality">{axes.map(axis => <a href={`${DOC}#${axis.anchor}`} class="surface-card workflow-card card-link arch-card"><CardHeading title={axis.name} linkArrow><axis.icon slot="icon" aria-hidden="true" /></CardHeading><p>{axis.how}</p></a>)}</div>
    <table class="reference-table arch-coverage" tabindex="0" aria-label="Backends for each capability contract"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Contract</th><th scope="col">Backends</th><th scope="col">Coverage</th></tr></thead><tbody>{neutrality.contracts.map(c => <tr class={c.green ? undefined : 'arch-gap'}><td><code>{c.contract.replace(/^contract:/, '')}</code></td><td>{c.vendors.length ? c.vendors.join(', ') : 'Any backend'}</td><td>{coverage(c)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
    <div class="link-row"><a href={DOC}>How Magpie achieves vendor neutrality</a><a href={`${DOC}#vendor-neutrality-score`}>How the score is computed</a><a href={`${DOC}#authoring-your-own-adapter`}>Write an adapter</a><a href="/tools">Browse tools</a></div>
  </section>
  <section id="organizations">
    <h2>Keep your project’s conventions</h2>
    <p>Most tool choices are the same for every project under one governing organization: every ASF project allocates CVEs the same way, reads the same mail archive and gates on PMC membership. An organization profile holds those shared defaults once: its governance vocabulary, the backend each capability uses, and its identity. A project names its organization and inherits the rest; its own configuration still wins, then the organization, then the framework default. The same skill runs unchanged for an ASF project and an independent one; the organization carries the difference.</p>
    <div class="arch-orgs">{data.organizations.map(org => <article class="surface-card arch-org"><h3>{ORG_LOGO[org.id] && <img src={ORG_LOGO[org.id]} alt="" width="24" height="24" />}{org.name}</h3><p>{orgSummary(org)}</p></article>)}</div>
    <p>Any foundation, company or collective can add its own: contribute it to the framework so its projects and others reuse it, keep it in the organization’s own repository, or keep one locally in a project’s overrides.</p>
    <div class="link-row"><a href={`${DOC}#organizations`}>How organizations work</a><a href="/docs/extending#who-extends-what">Who extends what</a><a href="/docs/extending">Extend Magpie</a><a href="https://github.com/apache/magpie/tree/main/organizations" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Organization profiles</a></div>
  </section>
  <section id="model"><h2>Explore the reference</h2><p>The capability and tool definitions below come from the framework. Implementation status and supported vendors are available in the tools directory.</p><div class="link-row"><a href="/docs/labels-and-capabilities">Labels and capabilities </a><a href="/docs/adapters/registry">Adapter registry </a><a href="/docs/skill-sources/authoring-a-source">External skill sources </a></div></section>
  <details id="tool-capabilities"><summary>Capability contracts</summary><table class="reference-table" tabindex="0" aria-label="Capability contracts"><tbody>{Object.entries(data.contracts).map(([name,description])=><tr><td><code>{name}</code></td><td>{description}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></details>
  <details id="skill-capabilities"><summary>Low-level capabilities</summary><table class="reference-table" tabindex="0" aria-label="Low-level capabilities"><tbody>{Object.entries(data.substrates).map(([name,description])=><tr><td><code>{name}</code></td><td>{description}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></details>
</ContentLayout>
